  "details": "In a lot of worlds, particularly Udon ones, I am not able to do certain things. Pressing certain buttons, controlling the airplanes in test pilots etc.\nI suppose this is because the world creator didn't specifically put in support for the controllers.   (There certainly are few people masochistic enough to attempt playing on the Vive Focus Plus like me. I believe most people don't even know VRC supports it). \nMaybe the problem could be solved via some generic translation of buttons, or a more generic way of taking controller inputs in Udon? (The former seems more realistic, as it doesn't involve having world creators make changes to worlds) \n\nAt the very least having the trigger button work would make some unplayable worlds playable.",
